      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I still remember my first Wimbledon in 1982—it was also my first time working there as a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "line judge",
            "zh": "司线裁判"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Since then, I’ve only missed two "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tournaments",
            "zh": "锦标赛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But next year, everything will change. An AI system will take our place. I felt "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "heartbroken",
            "ref": "v-heartbroken"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " when I heard the news."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When I was young, I loved playing tennis. During one Wimbledon, I saw an ad from the Professional Tennis "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Umpires",
            "zh": "裁判员"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Federation. They were looking for new members. I decided to try, and after just 30 minutes of training, I got the job. The PTUF had very high "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "standards",
            "ref": "v-standard"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". We had to stand and walk in certain ways on the court."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The pay wasn’t high, but we didn’t do it for money—we did it for the love of tennis. You started at small events and slowly moved up. Being chosen for Wimbledon was a dream come true for every tennis lover. Now, some of my "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "colleagues",
            "ref": "v-colleague"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " won’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "renew",
            "ref": "v-renew"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "licenses",
            "ref": "v-license"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " since they can’t work at Wimbledon anymore. I’m worried that smaller tournaments will soon have trouble finding line judges."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A human judge brings something special to the game. We help keep traditions alive and make the court feel complete. When "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "spectators",
            "ref": "v-spectator"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " watch a discussion between the line judge and the umpire, they learn more about tennis. All of this will be lost."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Of course, humans make mistakes sometimes. But we always try our best to be fair. Fairness means everything to us."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It’s sad to think I won’t work at Wimbledon again. I’ll always love tennis, but I don’t think I can go back just as a spectator—it wouldn’t feel the same."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
